MID_EV30_010_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_010_m01_001: 'Twould seem a gate of the underworld is belching\nforth foes again.
MID_EV30_010_m01_002: We have our next target. Let us set about our work\nwith renewed vigor.
MID_EV30_010_m01_003: We must not waste this chance to destroy the gate if\nwe hope to someday defeat Balor.
MID_EV30_010_m01_071: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_072: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_073: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_074: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_075: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_076: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_077: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_078: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_079: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_004: <NCA>"We'll get it done."
MID_EV30_010_m01_005: <NCB>"I don't know if I can do this."
MID_EV30_010_m01_070: <ACA>
MID_EV30_010_m01_006: <ACA>That's the spirit we need! We'll be following you \non this, Promised One.
MID_EV30_010_m01_007: <ACA>Your confidence serves as an inspiration to us all.
MID_EV30_010_m01_082: <ACB>
MID_EV30_010_m01_008: <ACB>You can't lose your nerve now, Promised One.\nThere are too many people counting on you.
MID_EV30_010_m01_009: <ACB>The time for angst is long past, I should think. Our\npresent moment calls only for action.
MID_EV30_010_m01_010: By the way, what are the Brimstone Lords and the\nrisen dead?
MID_EV30_010_m01_011: Like that last one we fought. Was that an actual\nperson? Or some kind of imitation?
MID_EV30_010_m01_012: 'Tis the authentic soul brought back to unlife. But the\nrisen dead do not reason as the living do.
MID_EV30_010_m01_013: Now, not to dwell on the subject, but I want you to\nbear in mind something about the risen dead.
MID_EV30_010_m01_014: A living soul's reason grants it self-recognition,\nsurvival instincts, and the desire for a legacy.
MID_EV30_010_m01_015: But our foes are unnatural parodies of life, intruding\nfrom the underworld into our world.
MID_EV30_010_m01_016: They are not motivated by the same reason that\nanimates you and me.
MID_EV30_010_m01_017: A living soul might crave sustenance, or sleep,\nor romance, or familial bonds.
MID_EV30_010_m01_018: But all of these have been replaced in our foes with\nhatred for the living and an urge to kill.
MID_EV30_010_m01_019: Even if they were once your parents or siblings,\nyou cannot expect to find common ground now.
MID_EV30_010_m01_020: Ngh...
MID_EV30_010_m01_021: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_022: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_023: While we are here, I may as well tell you more\nabout Balor.
MID_EV30_010_m01_024: He is one pillar among a special group of her\nchildren, also known as Founders.
MID_EV30_010_m01_025: There are seven such pillars, or Founders, including\nthat accursed boor Dagda.
MID_EV30_010_m01_026: Each was assigned a task. To Balor went the vital\nrole of purifying souls.
MID_EV30_010_m01_027: 'Twas his lot to take souls sullied by hatred and\nresentment into the underworld within himself.
MID_EV30_010_m01_028: Once they had been purified there, they would in\ntime return to the great cycle.
MID_EV30_010_m01_029: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_030: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_031: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_032: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_033: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_034: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_035: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_036: But taking in these souls placed upon Balor a\nheavy burden.
MID_EV30_010_m01_037: It may have been overmuch to expect even of\na Founder.
MID_EV30_010_m01_038: Especially at the Great Undoing, when masses of\nsouls would have flowed into him at once.
MID_EV30_010_m01_039: That may have marked the start of his descent\ninto madness.
MID_EV30_010_m01_040: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_041: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_042: When Balor's rage could no longer be contained,\nhe turned on his family.
MID_EV30_010_m01_043: He lashed out even at she who reigns at the pinnacle\nof the family—Sothis, the progenitor god.
MID_EV30_010_m01_044: But he was impotent before her and found himself\nbound for his troubles.
MID_EV30_010_m01_045: As punishment, she carved Balor's body into\neight pieces.
MID_EV30_010_m01_046: Each piece was placed in a container, all of which\nwere sealed in a tomb at the Veil of the Void.
MID_EV30_010_m01_047: You speak, then, of the Isle of Sorrows and its\ntemple of Balor.
MID_EV30_010_m01_048: From these eight pieces came what we know today\nas Drake's treasures.
MID_EV30_010_m01_049: A question for you. This progenitor god, Sothis...\nIs she truly so strong?
MID_EV30_010_m01_050: If you think yourself capable of standing against her,\nyour imagination exceeds your reach.
MID_EV30_010_m01_051: Though if you had skill enough to cleave the moon,\nperhaps then you could give her a moment's pause.
MID_EV30_010_m01_052: Ah— You mean to say that the claws of\nthis progenitor god can reach even the moon?
MID_EV30_010_m01_053: You think too small. 'Twould be closer to the mark to\nsay she could crush the moon in her jaws.
MID_EV30_010_m01_054: Ahhhh.
MID_EV30_010_m01_055: Now that he's been resurrected, I've no doubt that\nBalor hungers for revenge on her.
MID_EV30_010_m01_056: With the power he stands to gain from turning our\nworld into his domain, he will challenge her again.
MID_EV30_010_m01_057: Little does he realize that even with such power at\nhis beck, Balor is still a flea before her.
MID_EV30_010_m01_058: One would think he learned this lesson during their\nfirst bout, but...ah well.
MID_EV30_010_m01_059: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_060: The deeper threat is that in challenging her, he may\nawake her from slumber.
MID_EV30_010_m01_061: 'Twould bring about another Great Undoing, as dire\nas the one that last befell this planet.
MID_EV30_010_m01_080: Driven by defensive instincts, she would scorch the\nworld's surface and boil its seas dry.
MID_EV30_010_m01_081: Even after Balor was no more, she would rage on\nuntil this planet was unsuited to life.
MID_EV30_010_m01_062: Therefore, she commanded her children to do all that\nis necessary to prevent this.
MID_EV30_010_m01_063: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_064: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_065: 
MID_EV30_010_m01_066: Urgh... The scale of all this... I'm starting to\nget a headache.
MID_EV30_010_m01_067: But I understand what it is you're saying. We carry a\nheavy responsibility on our shoulders.
MID_EV30_010_m01_068: This ought to be a matter for her children. I am sorry\nthat you humans became involved.
MID_EV30_010_m01_069: But involved you are, and the fate of this world now\nrests with you.
