MID_EV30_114_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_114_m01_001: Huh?
MID_EV30_114_m01_002: <NCA>"Did you hear something?"
MID_EV30_114_m01_003: <NCB>"Are you tired?"
MID_EV30_114_m01_004: <ACA>Just now, I thought I heard her song.
MID_EV30_114_m01_005: <ACB>Not at all. But I thought I heard her singing.
MID_EV30_114_m01_006: Perhaps she's calling out to someone, as she did\nwith you.
MID_EV30_114_m01_007: Do you recall meeting her? 'Twould have been before\nyou woke up.
MID_EV30_114_m01_008: She called you back to wakefulness and gave you\na chance to atone.
MID_EV30_114_m01_009: Is that curiosity I spy on your face? Do you wonder\nif I'm different from the other children?
MID_EV30_114_m01_010: 'Tis no great surprise you should think so. I am\nsomewhat special.
MID_EV30_114_m01_011: <NCA>"Fortuna...are you the progenitor god?"
MID_EV30_114_m01_012: <NCB>"Special how?"
MID_EV30_114_m01_013: <ACA>Not in the way you mean. I'm no more than a mere\nsimulacrum of the progenitor god.
MID_EV30_114_m01_014: You may have guessed as much, but to say I'm\nDagda's daughter is to twist the truth.
MID_EV30_114_m01_015: One stark difference between me and my siblings\nis that I was not of woman born.
MID_EV30_114_m01_016: I am something of a synthesis between the tissue of\nthe progenitor god and that accursed boor Dagda.
MID_EV30_114_m01_017: My original purpose was to be a vessel for her soul.
MID_EV30_114_m01_018: And I am not alone in this. Several other such\nsimulacra walk this world.
MID_EV30_114_m01_019: They monitor the lands ruled by each Founder, just\nas I do for the land of Dagda.
MID_EV30_114_m01_020: Through me, she retains awareness of the state\nof this land.
MID_EV30_114_m01_021: Indeed, she knows what's happening in Dagda now.\nAnd she sees your efforts to combat it.
MID_EV30_114_m01_022: Here's a secret. Many of her children believe they\nhave seen the progenitor god themselves.
MID_EV30_114_m01_023: But in fact, that is only another of her simulacra\nthat housed her mind long, long ago.
MID_EV30_114_m01_024: <NCA>"I didn't know that."
MID_EV30_114_m01_025: And why would you? That sort of knowledge is\ntypically reserved for Founders.
MID_EV30_114_m01_026: The throne of the progenitor god in the holy land\nis positioned at the point closest to her original soul.
MID_EV30_114_m01_027: If a simulacrum like me were to sit on it, her soul\nwould flow into them with terrible force.
MID_EV30_114_m01_028: Whatever mind I possess would be snuffed out in\nfavor of her true self.
MID_EV30_114_m01_029: Do you follow? My nature ties me strongly to\nher soul.
MID_EV30_114_m01_030: 'Tis the reason I bear the same Diadem and wield\npower similar to hers.
MID_EV30_114_m01_031: But a vessel must contain a soul. I can, for now, call\nthe soul that animates me my own.
MID_EV30_114_m01_032: It frightens me to think that I might be swallowed\nup by the essence of the progenitor god.
MID_EV30_114_m01_033: The prospect of ceasing to be is as terrifying as it\nis unimaginable.
MID_EV30_114_m01_034: I find myself reluctant to serve the purpose I was\nonce created for...
MID_EV30_114_m01_035: Hm...
MID_EV30_027_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_027_m01_080: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_081: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_082: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_083: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_084: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_085: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_086: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_087: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_001: Ugh...
MID_EV30_027_m01_002: What a dismal spot to find a gate of the underworld.
MID_EV30_027_m01_003: It does seem like a pretty empty place. What\nhappened here?
MID_EV30_027_m01_004: Other than the gate, I just see sand and ruins.
MID_EV30_027_m01_005: I suppose you wouldn't know the significance of the\nplace without a keen interest in history.
MID_EV30_027_m01_006: The irony of the location is not lost on me, at least.
MID_EV30_027_m01_007: <NCA>"I know this place..."
MID_EV30_027_m01_008: Yes, 'tis the plains of Tarvos. Its history dates back\nto before the founding of the Dagdan Empire.
MID_EV30_027_m01_009: At that time, 'twas inhabited by a people who had\ninherited their civilization from the ancients.
MID_EV30_027_m01_010: I believe they were called Iskandariyans.
MID_EV30_027_m01_011: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_012: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_013: Their advanced technology gave rise to a mammoth\ncity in this region.
MID_EV30_027_m01_014: From there, they controlled large swathes of\nNorthern Dagda.
MID_EV30_027_m01_015: 'Twas inevitable that Dagda would have to contend\nwith them to solidify his rule.
MID_EV30_027_m01_016: Dagda told them to abandon their knowledge of the\npast, but their defiance was too deeply rooted.
MID_EV30_027_m01_017: The two factions clashed here at Tarvos, and Dagda's\nchildren won the day.
MID_EV30_027_m01_018: The Battle of Tarvos. I've heard the name.
MID_EV30_027_m01_019: But I never imagined those were the circumstances\nbehind it.
MID_EV30_027_m01_020: A people possessing forgotten knowledge of the\npast... They were doubtless formidable.
MID_EV30_027_m01_021: A shame they are gone. I hunger to fight them.
MID_EV30_027_m01_022: There are many places across this continent where\nruins older than the Great Undoing persist.
MID_EV30_027_m01_023: They are proof that our ancestors fought against\nthe gods for an age.
MID_EV30_027_m01_024: That little history note would explain why so many\nancient relics are uncovered around here.
MID_EV30_027_m01_025: I know merchants who would give a little more than\ntheir left arm just to own an Iskandariyan artifact.
MID_EV30_027_m01_026: Hmmm...
MID_EV30_027_m01_027: Does something not strike you as peculiar?
MID_EV30_027_m01_028: Here we are before a gate of the underworld, and yet\nthere are no risen dead in sight.
MID_EV30_027_m01_029: <NCA>"What do you make of that?"
MID_EV30_027_m01_030: I don't know. It could be a trap, or it could be\nnothing. I'm unsure what to expect.
MID_EV30_027_m01_031: I have to wonder if we could easily smash the gate\nnow, while we have the chance.
MID_EV30_027_m01_032: Our mission starts and ends with destroying\nthe gate, right?
MID_EV30_027_m01_033: No one's here. I'd say we should do it now.
MID_EV30_027_m01_034: Something nags at me, but no matter. Let's destroy\nthe gate and have done with this place.
MID_EV30_027_m01_035: Ah! What?!
MID_EV30_027_m01_036: <NCA>Grab Fortuna's hand.
MID_EV30_027_m01_037: I appreciate that. Of all the possible vectors of\nattack, I hadn't expected it from below.
MID_EV30_027_m01_038: Hm. So. I failed to slay even a single beast.
MID_EV30_027_m01_039: An unusual tactic—to rise from the sand beneath\nour feet.
MID_EV30_027_m01_040: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_041: You...as I recall, you were part of the Order\nof Mithras.
MID_EV30_027_m01_042: I will not suffer you to live.
MID_EV30_027_m01_043: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_044: So the guardians we face include my distant\nancestors, unjustly slain by Dagda the Great.
MID_EV30_027_m01_045: 'Tis fitting, in a sense, to be opposed here by\nghosts of the past.
MID_EV30_027_m01_046: Perhaps those of her children who still live have\ntheir own causality to reckon with.
MID_EV30_027_m01_047: Defenders of this queen of beasts. She who wrought\nthe Great Undoing by her own hand. Hear me now.
MID_EV30_027_m01_048: We own this world.
MID_EV30_027_m01_049: If not for the Great Undoing, we would still reign\nsupreme.
MID_EV30_027_m01_050: Shenlo, you are a Mediator of Nuwa... You were\ncreated with a duty just like me.
MID_EV30_027_m01_051: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_052: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_053: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_054: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_055: The Great Undoing was not a deliberate act on\nher part.
MID_EV30_027_m01_056: What followed from it is her karma to bear,\nand ours as well.
MID_EV30_027_m01_057: I admit as much. But even more dire circumstances\npress upon us now.
MID_EV30_027_m01_058: If we don't stop Balor's underworld from swallowing\nthis land, we shall see a second Great Undoing.
MID_EV30_027_m01_059: Once we have secured victory here, we will go forth\nand devour the rest of the world.
MID_EV30_027_m01_060: All those who think of themselves as gods will\nbe undone.
MID_EV30_027_m01_061: The world will be restored to a vast and\nperfect nothingness.
MID_EV30_027_m01_062: We care nothing for Balor's will. This battle is\nours alone.
MID_EV30_027_m01_063: Those who persist beyond this battle will become the\nheirs of this new world.
MID_EV30_027_m01_064: We do not recognize you "gods." You are as beasts to\nus, and we will destroy you and your defenders.
MID_EV30_027_m01_065: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_066: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_067: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_068: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_069: I can only see you as our enemy.
MID_EV30_027_m01_070: Though I revere my ancestors, I will not put the\nliving at risk on their behalf.
MID_EV30_027_m01_071: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_072: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_073: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_079: 
MID_EV30_027_m01_074: <NCA>"You'll go no farther."
MID_EV30_027_m01_075: Hear, hear. While I sympathize with your grievance,\nI can't endorse it.
MID_EV30_027_m01_076: We can't dwell on the past when the present asks\nall we have to give.
MID_EV30_027_m01_077: We've sworn an oath to protect what remains of this\nworld. Those things are not for you to devour.
MID_EV30_027_m01_078: Come, ghosts of the past. Let's settle accounts here\nonce and for all!
MID_EV30_028_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_028_m01_001: Grr... How can the beasts halt our advance...
MID_EV30_028_m01_089: 
MID_EV30_028_m01_090: 
MID_EV30_028_m01_091: 
MID_EV30_028_m01_092: 
MID_EV30_028_m01_093: 
MID_EV30_028_m01_094: 
MID_EV30_028_m01_095: 
MID_EV30_028_m01_096: 
MID_EV30_028_m01_097: 
MID_EV30_028_m01_098: 
MID_EV30_028_m01_099: 
MID_EV30_028_m01_002: The heavens do not recognize us as the true\ninheritors of this world? 
MID_EV30_028_m01_003: <NCA>"It's time to give up."
MID_EV30_028_m01_004: People of the ancient world... 'Tis hubris to claim\nthat you "ruled" in your day.
MID_EV30_028_m01_005: For this world has never belonged to anyone.
MID_EV30_028_m01_006: The only distinction is between who came first\nand who arrived later.
MID_EV30_028_m01_007: To "own" land is based on nothing more than lines\non a map—ones that anyone could draw.
MID_EV30_028_m01_008: 'Tis truly yours neither to claim nor to consume.
MID_EV30_028_m01_009: Right. Even back in Ribeira, people fought over the\nboundaries of their fields.
MID_EV30_028_m01_010: Sometimes they threw punches. But in the end\neveryone ate a meal together and made up.
MID_EV30_028_m01_011: Cai...this is much more consequential than farmers\narguing over where they can put crops.
MID_EV30_028_m01_012: It's important to talk things out.
MID_EV30_028_m01_013: How many lost their lives during the Great Undoing,\nhm? Allow me to remind you.
MID_EV30_028_m01_014: Five billion—or was it ten billion?—were burned to\ncinders before they knew what was happening.
MID_EV30_028_m01_015: Ngh...
